            0.83,
            0.142
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "5.2 What Can a Force Do to the Objects on Which It Is Applied?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.153,
            0.883,
            0.21
          ],
          "content": "We experience push or pull in our daily lives all the time, often without even realising it. Let us recall some of these experiences and **analyse** them."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.268,
            0.228,
            0.624,
            0.253
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 5.2: Let us analyse"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.273,
            0.271,
            0.882,
            0.31
          ],
          "content": "**Think** of situations where a force (push or pull) is applied and list them in Table 5.1."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.273,
            0.314,
            0.883,
            0.371
          ],
          "content": "z Analyse each situation and write the effect of the force in Table 5.1. Some situations and their effects are already listed for you."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.135,
            0.413,
            0.888,
            0.663
          ],
          "content": "| S.No. | Action Push/Pull | Effect |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1. | Your friend holding Pull your moving bicycle from behind to stop it | Stopping or decreasing the speed of the bicycle |\n| 2. | Hitting a moving ball Push with a bat | Changing the direction of a moving ball |\n| 3. | Pressing an inflated Push balloon………………… ………………… | Change in shape of the balloon………………… |",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.297,
                0.387,
                0.801,
                0.41
              ],
              "content": "~~Table 5.1: Different actio~~ns and their effects"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_2_table_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.675,
            0.883,
            0.734
          ],
          "content": "What do you **conclude** from these examples? Does a force cause a moving object to stop? Can it change speed, or direction of motion, or change the shape of an object?"
        },
